\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Brazil's Neves would end  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  swap program, adviser says\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alonso Soto and Jeferson Ribeiro  \par \uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2014\par 22:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Oct 15 (Reuters) - Brazilian presidential candidate Aecio Neves will end a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap program that has cushioned losses in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, if he is elected later this month, Neves's choice for finance minister, Arminio Fraga, told Reuters on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Neves, a centrist who has promised to rescue the economy from recession, is running neck-and-neck with left-leaning President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  in Brazil's tightest presidential election in at least two decades.\par \par \uc2 Fraga, a former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief whom Neves has said will be his finance minister, said the program would end immediately and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stock of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps would be wound down as contracts expire.\par \par \uc2 "We would certainly not have that program," Fraga said in a telephone interview. "The government is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that should not happen except in times of great uncertainty. The best policy for Brazil is to have a free-floating exchange rate."\par \par \uc2 Since last August, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivatives designed to support the real.\par \par \uc2 Fraga, a Princeton-educated economist, said that Neves would likely include academics and market economists in the next \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board if he is elected. (Reporting by Alonso Soto; Editing by Peter Galloway)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-18T20:22:27.000Z  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141015eaaf00nm1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
