\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Likely to Avoid  \highlight22\uc2 FX Interventions \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2014\par 13:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 7:37 EDT - \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to avoid a heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, despite the drastic depreciation of the Brazilian real, in order to not increase a speculative wave against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Sidnei Nehme, director of the NGO \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerage in Sao Paulo. On Monday, the real traded around 2.45 to the dollar, after closing at 2.4124 on Friday. The real depreciation came as recent political polls showed incumbent President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  gaining ground versus her main contender Marina Silva. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1119 GMT \uc2 Sweden's National Debt Office\uc2  will auction its June 2022 and May 2025-dated bonds Wednesday, with the latter being the current Swedish 10-year benchmark, while the 2022-dated one an "off-the-run" or non-benchmark bond, last reopened in late 2012. Reopening non-benchmark bonds is a regular practice among national debt agencies, and tends to happen either on primary dealers' particular request or because the debt agency wants to boost its outstanding volume to smooth its redemption profile. "The NDO has always discussions with market makers ahead of the auction and it seems market makers have argued for the June 2022 bond," says Jussi Hiljanen, head of fixed income research at SEB. "There's nothing strange with that," he says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1112 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision to keep the interest rate on hold has put the ball in the government's court to deliver on structural reforms to lift growth and contain inflation, says HSBC Global Research in a note. RBI is likely to retain its current stance for the foreseeable future, while the government plays a stronger role in boosting growth and removing supply-side bottlenecks. "Eventually, this may pave the way for gradual monetary policy easing," it says. Since food inflation is mostly supply-led, the house believes it is a "subtle nudge" for the central government to move quickly on reforms. Earlier in the day, RBI kept its key repo rate unchanged at 8%. (nupur.acharya@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1102 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 's monetary policy statement was tweaked in a slightly dovish direction, with risks to its 8% retail inflation now more slanted to the downside, says Mole Hau, Asia economist with \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a note. The RBI earlier in the day kept its key policy rate unchanged, remaining watchful of the inflation trajectory. A RBI chart projected retail inflation to be a full percentage point above its 6% target by early 2016, a fact "downplayed" in the policy statement and the press conference. The chances of a rate cuts remains dim if RBI is serious about keeping inflation on its desired path down to 6% by early 2016, the note says. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's "sophistry" is understandable, as a more explicit view that inflation risks remain could be viewed "provocative" to the government and financial markets, it says. (nupur.acharya@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1053 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Indian industry lobby groups on Tuesday said they understood the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision to keep interest rates steady to guard against inflation. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  kept its benchmark lending rate unchanged on Tuesday in its bi-monthly monetary policy. "Although the upside risks to inflation have eased, the RBI has chosen to take a cautious stance given the geo-political risks that could have a bearing on oil prices and the lagged full impact of skewed rainfall which could impact food prices," says A. Didar Singh, secretary general of FICCI, an industry body. India's retail inflation was at 7.80% in August. The RBI wants it to be below 8% by January and ease to 6% by January 2016. (prasanta.sahu@wsj.com, Twitter: @pksahu9) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1048 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's Finance Ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  says it is working with \f28 \uc2 \f2 JP Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  to sell dollar-denominated bonds to international markets. The company is also helping Vietnam to achieve an investment-grade credit ratings by 2020, the ministry says following a meeting Tuesday between Deputy Finance Minister Truong Chi Trung and \f28 \uc2 \f2 JP Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Asia-Pacific chief executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nicolas Aguzin\f28 \uc2 \f2 . A government official said earlier this month Vietnam plans to raise $1 billion by selling dollar-denominated bonds in international markets later this year. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  in July raised Vietnam's sovereign rating by one notch, to B1 from B2, with a stable outlook, citing the country's record of macroeconomic stability. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; Twitter: @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1029 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The ECB's monetary policy is correct, says ECB Governing Council member \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ewald Nowotny\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "I believe the policy that the ECB is following...is right," he said at a conference in Vienna on banking supervision. Mr. Nowotny's comments come just two days before the ECB is due to meet at its next monetary policy meeting in Naples, Italy. The ECB is expected to announce more details about its purchase program for asset-backed securities and covered bonds. (todd.buell@wsj.com; @ToddBuell) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1013 GMT The euro-forint declined again over the past 24 hours, in line with other emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , induced by expectations of this week's ECB meeting where market participants expect further monetary easing, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. The U.S. Fed isn't quick with its tightening policy, another factor that could boost emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes however that 310 may be a strong resistance level for EUR/HUF, while Erste says it could approach an important level at 308, which is the 200-day moving average. EUR/HUF is at 310.23 versus 311.25 late Monday. (veronika.gulyas@wsj.com; @VeronikaGulyas1) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0957 GMT The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norges Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's announcement that it will buy NOK250 million per day starting October 1 is a major turning point for the Norwegian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The NOK buying reflects that taxes paid in NOK and the dividend from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Statoil\f28 \uc2 \f2  are no longer enough to cover the oil-adjusted deficit, forcing the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norges Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to tap into the proceeds in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the State's Direct Financial Interest. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norges Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to continue buying NOK in November at a similar daily amount, which will take the yearly purchases to NOK10 billion. EUR/NOK slumped to 8.11 from around 8.18 Tuesday; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske\f28 \uc2 \f2  is looking for a break of the 8.0967 September low to target 7.95. (gary.stride@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0955 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Indonesia's defense spending more than tripled under outgoing President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono\f28 \uc2 \f2 , but the country still finds itself part-way through a long-term program to build a "Minimum Essential Force" capable of defending Indonesia's sprawling maritime territory. Ristian Atriandi Supriyanto, a research fellow at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 S. Rajaratnam School of International Studies\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore, said that President-elect Joko Widodo has signaled his commitment to the Minimum Essential Force program, but also a desire "to go beyond the MEF". That would necessitate further defense budget increases and some big-ticket procurements, with South Korea potentially first in line to benefit, having already secured Indonesian orders for new jets and submarines. "South Korea has shown itself to be the most viable defense partner for Indonesia," Supriyanto observed. (trefor.moss@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0954 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Hong Kong stock market went from bad to worse in September, capping on Tuesday its worst month since May 2012 with a 7.3% slide in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index. Uncertainty over the future of U.S. interest-rate policy and China's bumpy economy had dragged on stocks from the start of September, with pro-democracy protests that flared over the weekend in Hong Kong spurring further selling. Investors "are still trading, but obviously quite cautious", says Jesse Lentchner, Asia-Pacific chief executive officer for the brokerage firm BTIG. "Between the month end, quarter end, upcoming holiday, and then of course the Occupy movement, no one wants to take on additional risk." (mia.lamar@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0952 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The U.S dollar took a breather Tuesday afternoon in Asia as its longest rally slowed down, as the ICE DXY U.S. Dollar Index fell as much as 0.36%. The U.S. dollar continued to trade near four-year highs, against a basket of six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "There were further signs of volatility as the U.S. market bounced around. With no macro data of merit, U.S. and European investors watched the developing political escalations in Hong Kong," Evan Lucas, market strategist at IG Markets wrote in a note Tuesday. The slowing U.S. dollar helped pare losses in the Australian dollar and the New Zealand dollar, which had plummeted over the past few days. (Anjani.Trivedi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 30, 2014 07:37 ET (11:37 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140930ea9u001gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
