\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real firms after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  steps up  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2014\par 14:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Sept 24 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real gained modestly on Wednesday as uncertainty about the outcome of the October presidential elections eclipsed the impact of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision to step up its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real gained 0.1 percent in early trade and hovered around the 2.40 per dollar mark. On Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had weakened past that level for the first time in seven months.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had slid more than 3 percent during five consecutive sessions of losses through Tuesday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to increase the rollover pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps that expire early next month to support the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The real has been weakening as President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2 , who investors accuse of failing to keep inflation at bay and driving the economy into a recession, regains voter support in the latest opinion polls. (Reporting by Walter Brandimarte Editing by W Simon) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-9-24T13:15:47.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140924ea9o00dg0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
