\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Increases  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2014\par 13:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped to the lowest level since mid-February.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that it will increase the pace of rollovers of dollar swaps starting in Wednesday's session. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will offer investors the rollover of up to 15,000 swap contracts at daily auction, compared with 6,000 contacts offered in previous sessions. The increase represents $750 million, compared with $300 million previously.\par \par \uc2 The swap auction is the equivalent of the sale of dollars in the futures markets. The futures market in Brazil for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is about eight times bigger than the spot market. Only 14 major banks are allowed to operate in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, severely restricting access to the market and pushing a majority of players into the futures market.\par \par \uc2 In the most recent session, the Brazilian real closed at 2.408 reais to the dollar, the lowest level since Feb. 12, when the real closed at 2.42 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost ground in recent sessions as certain polls showed incumbent president \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  gaining ground versus her main contender Marina Silva, ahead of October's election.\par \par \uc2 Two polls released Tuesday showed Ms. Rousseff ahead of Ms. Silva for the first time since mid-August, though the two are still in a technical tie.\par \par \uc2 Investors say Ms. Rousseff's policies are too \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and financial markets in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  have usually reacted negatively to good polling news for the incumbent. Shares in state-controlled companies have been especially sensitive to poll results.\par \par \uc2 The biggest decliner in the Ibovespa in Tuesday's session was Eletrobras, a state-controlled electric utility. The company's shares fell 2.9% to 10.18 reais. State-controlled oil company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  (PBR, PETR3.BR, PETR4.BR), the most heavily weighted company in the Ibovespa, was another big decliner, giving up 2.2% to 20.13 reais.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rogerio Jelmayer at rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 24, 2014 07:25 ET (11:25 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140924ea9o00189\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
