\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real at near 6-month lows,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2014\par 18:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Sept 15 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real dropped to\par its lowest level in nearly six months on Monday, testing the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's willingness to tolerate a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while\par the Colombian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthened the most since late July.\par     The real fell 0.6 percent to 2.3487 reais per dollar\par on investor concern over gains by President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dilma Rousseff\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a\par voter poll before next month's election. Investors are hopeful\par that a different administration would enact more market-friendly\par policies.\par     But traders were cautions about betting on a further decline\par in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the short term as they kept an eye on\par potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to limit further weakness in\par the real, which makes imports more expensive and contributes to\par inflation.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  returned to (weakened) levels where,\par historically, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has shown signs of discomfort, so\par the market remains cautious," said Reginaldo Galhardo, head of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at Sao Paulo brokerage Treviso.     \par     A government source told Reuters late Friday that the bank\par will extend its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program into 2015 and may\par increase the rollover pace of expiring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps to curb\par volatility in the real. \par     Colombia's peso strengthened for the first session in\par six and its most since late July after minutes from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's most recent policy-setting meeting, released late on\par Friday, showed some board members thought there was no need to\par continue raising interest rates. Colombian policymakers last\par raised the benchmark rate by 25 basis points to 5.5 percent.\par  \par     Analysts were divided over the outlook for interest rates in\par Colombia. Some, such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' Nader Nazmi, estimate the\par bank will likely pause its hiking cycle for the year to monitor\par its effects.\par     Others such as Nomura analyst Mario Castro see the bank\par implementing two more 25 basis point increases, citing Nomura's\par expectations for an increase in core inflation in the fourth\par quarter.\par     Chile's peso swung widely before settling slightly\par weaker in the afternoon.\par     Prices for copper, the country's main export,\par slipped towards three-month lows on Monday after data showed\par growth at China's factories stumbled to its weakest in nearly\par six years in August.\par     In equities markets, Brazil's Bovespa stock index \par recouped part of the previous session's losses. The gains were\par driven by steelmakers and iron-ore miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vale SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par after spot iron ore posted its biggest one-day rise since March\par on Monday.\par     The broader MSCI Latin American stock index \par posted its first rise in eight sessions, with Mexico's \f28 \uc2 \f2 IPC\f28 \uc2 \f2  stock\par index edging higher and Chile's IPSA stock index \par little-changed.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1515 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                   daily %    YTD %\par                                   change   change\par                       Latest              \par  MSCI Emerging          1054.33    -0.68     5.87\par  Markets                                  \par  MSCI LatAm             3406.53      0.1     6.33\par                                           \par  Brazil Bovespa         57267.5      0.6    11.18\par                                           \par  Mexico \f28 \uc2 \f2 IPC\f28 \uc2 \f2             45904.07     0.23     7.44\par                                           \par  Chile IPSA             3987.13     -0.1     7.78\par                                           \par  Chile IGPA            19377.24    -0.08     6.31\par                                           \par  Argentina MerVal     11143.869     0.81   106.71\par                                           \par  Colombia IGBC         14242.34     -0.2     8.96\par                                           \par  Peru IGRA             16966.75     0.24     7.70\par                                           \par  Venezuela IBC          2739.32     1.25     0.10\par                                           \par                                                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                       daily %    YTD %\par                                   change   change\par                          Latest           \par  Brazil real             2.3434    -0.36     0.57\par                                           \par  Mexico peso            13.2322     0.14    -1.53\par                                           \par  Chile peso               595.2    -0.54   -11.61\par                                           \par  Colombia peso             1985     0.55    -2.67\par                                  