\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank \highlight\uc2  to extend  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  program - gov't source\b0\par\par\uc2 155 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2014\par 22:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Sept 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will extend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program into 2015 and may increase the rollover pace of expiring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to curb volatility in the real, a source at President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2 's economic team said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The source told Reuters that the current \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, which includes the sale of as many as 4,000 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps per day to support the real, will not suffer changes this year.\par \par \uc2 The real on Friday closed 1.6 percent lower to 2.3349 per dollar, its weakest level in nearly 10 months, as anxiety about the country's October presidential election added to an environment of rising risk aversion fueled by fears of higher U.S. interest rates. (Reporting by Patricia Duarte, writing by Walter Brandimarte; Editing by Chris Reese)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-9-15T20:48:01.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140912ea9c00pjh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
