\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil election, U.S. rate fears weigh on Latam\b0\par\par\uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2014\par 21:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates with Brazilian markets adding to losses, adds comment\par from investor)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, Sept 12 (Reuters) - Brazilian financial markets\par slumped on Friday, leading losses among Latin American peers as\par anxiety related to the country's October presidential election\par added to an environment of rising risk aversion fueled by fears\par of higher U.S. interest rates.\par     The Brazilian real  slid more than 2 percent\par during the session to trade at its weakest level since mid March\par after yet another opinion survey, this time by the Ibope\par pollster, confirmed President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dilma Rousseff\f28 \uc2 \f2  and\par environmentalist Marina Silva were neck-and-neck in a vote\par expected to go to a second round on Oct. 26. \par     "The survey led investors to abandon the idea that Marina\par would continue to soar in opinion polls until the election day,"\par said Paulo Petrassi, a partner at Leme Investimentos in Brazil.\par "Now it's clear that this is going to be a highly disputed\par election."\par     Brazil's benchmark Bovespa stock index also lost\par more than 2 percent to trade at its lowest intraday level since\par mid-August as traders unwound optimistic bets they had been\par recently building.\par     Brazilian markets had posted sharp gains in previous weeks\par when initial polls showed Silva eventually defeating Rousseff,\par who is accused by investors of excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par economy.\par     Also hurting emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in general was a\par rise in yields on U.S. Treasuries resulting from fears that the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  may increase U.S. borrowing costs earlier than\par anticipated. Data showing U.S. retail sales rose broadly in\par August while consumer sentiment hit a 14-month high in September\par contributed to that perception. \par     Higher U.S. interest rates tend to attract money invested in\par higher yielding, riskier places.\par     "If those polls continue to show larger re-election chances\par for Rousseff and if the external scenario remains negative, we\par don't know how weak the real is going to be," said Marcos\par Trabbold, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader with B&T brokerage in Brazil.\par     Also fueling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses in Brazil was a Reuters report\par that a senior economic adviser for Silva said her government\par would eliminate a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program that has been\par adopted by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for about a year to support the\par real. \par     "Two factors are contributing to the rise in the dollar\par (against the real) today," said Brazilian-based Lerosa\par Investimentos in a research note. \par     "On the one hand, U.S. Treasuries yields are going up this\par morning ... on the other hand, there are remarks by an economic\par adviser from PSB (Silva's party) saying that they will stop the\par program of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," it said.\par     Speculation that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may act to stop the\par real from weakening much past 2.3 per dollar, which would have a\par negative impact on inflation, was growing among traders.\par     "If the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does not indicate that it will step up\par its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the market will keep putting pressure on\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader with a foreign brokerage who\par believes policymakers should soon increase the rollover rate of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps that expire early next month.\par     Elsewhere in Latin America, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Chile \par and Colombia weakened between 0.5 percent and 0.7\par percent. The Mexican peso recovered from early losses to\par trade nearly unchanged, however.\par \par  \par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1645 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                  daily %    YTD %\par                                  change   change\par                      Latest              \par  MSCI Emerging         1061.08    -0.78     6.66\par  Markets                                 \par  MSCI LatAm            3394.12    -2.88     9.18\par                                          \par  Brazil Bovespa       56839.87    -2.57    10.35\par                                          \par  Mexico \f28 \uc2 \f2 IPC\f28 \uc2 \f2            45722.19     0.11     7.01\par                                          \par  Chile IPSA            3999.13    -0.66     8.11\par                                          \par  Chile IGPA           19426.23    -0.57     6.58\par                                          \par  Argentina MerVal    11007.539     0.37   104.18\par                                          \par  Colombia IGBC        14255.92    -0.01     9.06\par                                          \par  Peru IGRA            16990.69     -0.5    