\par\par \b \uc2 Exclusive:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Silva would cut spending, end  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  program\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alonso Soto  \par \uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2014\par 00:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Reuters) - Marina Silva would push for large budget cuts and end a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  program aimed at supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if she is elected Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s next president in October, a senior economic adviser told Reuters on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Alexandre Rands, an economist who helped draft Silva's economic plan, said she could cut up to 100 billion reais ($43 billion) - or about 2 percent of gross domestic product - in budget spending next year to send a strong signal to investors worried about the deterioration of public finances.\par \par \uc2 "Our priority is not to cut spending for the sake of it. Our priority is to control inflation in order to create an environment that will allow Brazil to grow more," he said in an interview that provided some of the most specific guidance yet about Silva's financial policies.\par \par \uc2 Silva, an environmentalist whom polls show is running neck-to-neck with President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  in a likely runoff next month, has encouraged many investors with her market-friendly economic platform, which includes giving the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  full independence.\par \par \uc2 A sluggish economy and growing fiscal deficits during Rousseff's four years in office has cost Brazil a downgrade of its debt rating and scared off some investors who say the leftist leader is too \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rands said Silva would eliminate many of the economic distortions that have dragged the once-booming Brazilian economy into recession.\par \par \uc2 He mentioned the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  scheme, which has kept the real stronger since last year, as one of those distortions that will be corrected under Silva.\par \par \uc2 "That does not mean that you cannot carry out small, temporary actions to eliminate volatility," Rands said.\par \par \uc2 The real weakened slightly in late trading due to Rands' comments, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Since last August, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivatives designed to support the real.\par \par \uc2 LESS PORK\par \par \uc2 Rands, who runs an economic consultancy in the northeastern state of Pernambuco, is part of Silva's team of economic advisers, which also includes well-known economist Eduardo Giannetti da Fonseca.\par \par \uc2 He said the budget cuts would spare initiatives such as the Bolsa Familia welfare program for poor families, focusing instead on pork-barrel spending for projects in lawmakers' districts.\par \par \uc2 "There is a lot of fat that can be cut and the Marina (Silva) camp is sending positive signals on that fiscal front," said Alex Agostini, chief economist with Austin Rating. "It could generate a confidence shock that will allow the economy to grow more in the future."\par \par \uc2 Rands said a Silva administration would also aim to lower the center of Brazil's official inflation target below the current 4.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Economists complain that such a wide target range has allowed politicians to keep inflation high, hurting retailers and dragging down investments in Latin America's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 He said the campaign's economic team is debating whether to keep the current leadership at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or opt for a new team during the transition toward full independence if she is elected.\par \par \uc2 Rands was a macroeconomics classmate of current \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  at the \uc2 University of Illinois\uc2 , Urbana-Champaign.\par \par \uc2 "Brazil has a credibility problem. Once Rousseff is out of power part of that problem will be resolved," Rands said. "But we will need to win back credibility with the correct monetary and fiscal policies."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Alonso Soto; Editing by Diane Craft and Lisa Shumaker) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-9-11T22:59:02.000Z  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140911ea9b00mgd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
