\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's finmin disputes IMF report that economy is vulnerable\b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2014\par 03:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, July 29 (Reuters) - Brazilian Finance Minister Guido Mantega said on Tuesday that an \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  report that warns of the  vulnerability of the Brazilian economy makes no sense.               \par \par \uc2 In a report about risks to the global economy, the lender included Brazil in a list of emerging market countries with higher vulnerabilities. The IMF said that sluggish expansion in the developing world was increasingly likely due to structural, not cyclical, factors.               \par \par \uc2 "The report's conclusions that Brazil is fragile makes no sense," Mantega told reporters, adding that the lender is only repeating mistaken predictions made by market economists in recent months.               \par \par \uc2 In a separate report also published on Tuesday, the IMF said Brazil's external position is "moderately weaker" than fundamentals. The lender also said that the Brazilian real  was overvalued by between 5 percent and 15 percent in 2013 and that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not be used to resist \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressures.               \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the confidence of international markets and it's a solid country from the point of view of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange" Mantega said.               \par \par \uc2 Mantega said that the country's current account deficit - country's widest measurement of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows - should improve next year.               \par \par \uc2 Brazil's external deficit hit a record $81 billion last year due to a drop in global prices of key exports such as soy and iron ore and robust demand for imports.               \par \par \uc2 Fewer dollars in the local market has put downward pressure on the real.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since last year to keep the real from weakening too much and further stoking already high inflation.               \par \par \uc2 Mantega said that inflation in Brazil continues at "comfortable" levels and that government policies to control prices have been successful.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-7-30T02:10:06.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140730ea7u000jj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
