\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real up on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , U.S. data boosts risk appetite\b0\par\par\uc2 743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2014\par 18:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RIO DE JANEIRO, June 25 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real\par rallied on Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program will remain intact through the end\par of the year, while disappointing U.S. economic data boosted\par appetite for emerging market assets in general.\par     The real  gained 0.8 percent to 2.2066 per\par dollar after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced it will stick with its\par daily auctions of much as $200 million worth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps -\par the same amount of derivatives it currently offers to investors\par who seek protection against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses. \par     The bank introduced regular auctions of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps last\par August in one of its most successful initiatives to stabilize\par Brazil's volatile exchange rate. After strengthening in 2011 to\par levels that threatened local industry, the real weakened\par sharply in 2012-13, fueling inflation that has dragged on\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dilma Rousseff\f28 \uc2 \f2 's popularity.\par     The steady supply of swaps has helped the real gain about 6\par percent so far this year. During the past few months, the\par exchange rate has remained largely within a range of 2.2 to 2.5\par reais per dollar.\par     "The rationale behind that program is to keep the dollar\par within that range, helping curb inflation and reducing\par volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market," said Luiz Fernando G\u234\'00\'EAnova, a\par trader with the Daycoval bank in Sao Paulo.\par     G\u234\'00\'EAnova, as well as some other market players, were a bit\par surprised by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announcement. Many believed\par policymakers would take advantage of a period of relatively calm\par in global markets to wind down the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program, saving\par firepower for moments of stress.\par     Still, G\u234\'00\'EAnova said, the announcement "brings certainty that\par the daily offer (of swaps) will remain abundant."\par     Meanwhile, other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  posted more\par modest gains as investors bet the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will take time\par to raise interest rates after the U.S. economy contracted much\par more than expected in the first quarter. \par     Low interest rates in the world's largest economy usually\par boost investors' appetite for higher-yielding emerging market\par bonds.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Mexico and Chile each gained\par around 0.3 percent after the disappointing U.S. data.\par     Latin American stock markets suffered with the\par weaker-than-expected U.S. data, however, with MSCI's benchmark\par stock index for the region 0.1 percent lower.\par     Shares of Brazil's state-run oil company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleo Brasileiro\par SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 , continued to slide on concern that a\par government's decision to sell the company new oil rights will\par further weigh on its already large debt and weak performance.\par     Preferred shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 1.3 percent,\par adding to losses of 3.6 percent recorded on Tuesday, as analysts\par warned the strategy appeared to be a government attempt to\par transfer future \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2  profit to government coffers.\par  \par     "\f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' current problem is not the availability of oil\par fields to be explored, it is the lack of resources to explore\par them," analysts with Planner brokerage wrote in a research note.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2  weighed heavily on the Bovespa index,\par which dropped 0.6 percent. Other key stock indexes across Latin\par America posted a better performance: Mexico's \f28 \uc2 \f2 IPC\f28 \uc2 \f2  edged\par up 0.1 percent while Chile's IPSA declined 0.2 percent.\par     \par  \par     \par     Key Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and stock indexes at 1600 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                                 Daily     YTD \par                                                  pct      pct\par                                   Latest      change   change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets             1,043.26    -0.47     4.53\par  MSCI LatAm                        3,399.27    -0.05     6.25\par  Brazil Bovespa                   53,963.41    -0.58     4.77\par  Mexico \f28 \uc2 \f2 IPC\f28 \uc2 \f2                        42,921.72     0.09     0.46\par  Chile IPSA                         3,893.2    -0.23     5.24\par  Chile IGPA                       18,987.58    -0.18     4.17\par  Argentina MerVal                   7,944.1     0.39    47.36\par  Colombia IGBC                    14,195.88    -0.36     8.60\par  Peru IGRA                        16,515.87     0.15     4.84\par  Venezuela IBC                     2,136.91    -0.81   -21.91\par                                                              \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                     Daily     YTD \par   