\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil likely to wind down  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  program as real steadies\b0\par\par\uc2 By Walter Brandimarte   \par \uc2 702 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2014\par 20:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, June 16 (Reuters) - \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely scale back its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program within the next couple of weeks, hoping that a period of relative calm in global markets will help it unwind the plan without causing too much instability for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Brazil has tried a number of measures to stabilize its volatile exchange rate, which strengthened in 2011 to levels that threatened local industry but then weakened too fast in 2012-13, fueling inflation. Rising prices have hurt Brazilians' spending power, dragging down economic activity as well as President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2 's popularity.\par \par \uc2 In one of its most successful initiatives, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last August started daily auctions of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps.\par \par \uc2 The derivatives allow the bank to support the real without selling a single dollar from its $380 billion in foreign reserves. As a result, the real has been largely stable at between 2.2 and 2.3 per dollar in recent months.\par \par \uc2 But for the program to work, holders have to be able - at least in theory - to trade the swaps for cash in moments of crisis, which means the value of swaps in circulation cannot exceed the size of Brazil's foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts warn that the prudent threshold is much lower than that, and recommend policymakers curtail the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program even further. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already reduced the pace of sales in December, but the stock of swaps has since swollen to nearly $90 billion.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't sell swaps forever. It ought to use this instrument in specific situations," said M\u225\'00\'E1rcio Garcia, a visiting professor at \uc2 Stanford University\uc2  who has studied \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has been calm. It's not a moment for the bank to spend its dollar reserves or to sell derivatives that are backed by the reserves," added Garcia.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the real has gained more than 5 percent against the dollar. The gains are partly a result of the steady supply of swaps but also due to prospects that U.S. interest rates will not go up before mid-2015.\par \par \uc2 Unwinding the program has proved to be more difficult than it seems, however.\par \par \uc2 When the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tried to slow the rollover pace of expiring swaps earlier this month, the real slumped 1.5 percent in one day, forcing policymakers to backtrack.\par \par \uc2 The bank not only returned to its previous rollover pace, but it promised to keep offering swaps past June 30, an action aimed at killing speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program's days are numbered.\par \par \uc2 Details of the length and the magnitude of the extended program are still to be announced and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman declined to provide any new information.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the bank offers as many as 4,000 swaps worth $200 million in daily auctions, on top of 10,000 contracts to roll over expiring maturities.\par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program unchanged, rolling over 100 percent of expiring contracts, its stock of swaps would grow to more than $115 billion by the end of the year, \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  analysts estimated.\par \par \uc2 By continuously \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks excessive distortions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate that could deepen Brazil's economic problems, including a low investment rate and a current account deficit of nearly 4 percent of gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could slow its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the real is testing the 2.20-per-dollar area, said Win Thin, head of emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy with \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York. On Monday, it traded around 2.23 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Vail, head of fixed income at U.S. Bank Wealth Management, estimates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could still increase the amount of outstanding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps by 30 percent before investors get worried about the stock of these derivatives.\par \par \uc2 "There are always risks if they increase their exposure (to swaps) but I don't think it reached levels that are concerning the officials at this point," she said. (Reporting by Walter Brandimarte; Editing by Steve Orlofsky) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-16T19:53:16.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140616ea6g00n5f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
