\par\par \b \uc2 POLL- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  to extend  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 , Mexico peso to gain\b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2014\par 15:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * For poll details see\par \par \uc2 By Silvio Cascione and Jean Arce\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, June 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely extend beyond June its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to avoid any abrupt losses in the exchange rate, though it could reduce the size of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap sales, a Reuters poll showed.\par \par \uc2 Forecasts for the Brazilian real in Reuters' monthly survey of 31 strategists remained nearly unchanged. It points to a gradual weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar from the current 2.27 per dollar to 2.47 in 12 months.\par \par \uc2 The poll also showed prospects of slight gains for the Mexican peso over the next 12 months, while the Russian rouble and the Turkish lira are expected to weaken against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have benefitted recently from months of low volatility as the U.S. Federal Reserve tapers its monthly economic stimulus at a slow and predictable pace.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also played a key role in stabilizing local markets, as a deteriorating trade balance and concerns over the outcome of the October election would probably weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nine of the 11 who answered an extra question said they expect the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue offering a daily ration of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps after the end of this month, when the current \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program is scheduled to end.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability is crucial for Brazil as authorities struggle to keep inflation under control. Rising prices have dented President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2 's wide lead in the run-up for the October re-election campaign.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  programme is likely to be left intact," said \uc2 Michael Henderson\uc2 , Latin America economist at Maplecroft.\par \par \uc2 "With the prospect of further monetary tightening seemingly ruled out by weakening GDP growth and October's impending election, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management could play a critical role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to prevent a near-term acceleration of inflation."\par \par \uc2 Of the nine economists who said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would extend its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, five expect the bank to reduce the number of contracts offered per day. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offers an equivalent of $200 million per day currently.\par \par \uc2 Traders say the program has been successful in lowering volatility, keeping the real within an informal band of 2.20 to 2.25 for most of the past two months.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in Latin America, the Mexican peso is expected to gain slightly to 12.80 per dollar in 12 months from 12.95 currently, in a small improvement from the prior month's poll.\par \par \uc2 However, it remains far from the heights expected in early 2013, when President \uc2 Enrique Pena Nieto\uc2  started to work on an ambitious agenda of market-friendly reforms, especially in the oil sector.\par \par \uc2 "(The economy) has been too weak and it's all based on expectations. Macroeconomic data has not been strong enough yet to prop up the peso by year-end," said Carlos Ugalde, analyst at Signum Research, in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 The survey also predicted that Turkey's lira, which stabilised after a free fall that triggered an aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate rise earlier in the year, will weaken slightly to 2.22 per dollar in a year, from 2.11 currently.\par \par \uc2 The rand is seen at 10.63 per dollar in 12 months, just slightly firmer from 10.73, where it is trading currently. (Additional reporting by Seda Sezer and Vuyani Ndaba; Polling by Ishaan Gera and Diptarka Roy; Editing by Ross Finley and Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-7T13:22:18.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140604ea64009na\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
