\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil currency \highlight\uc2  sinks despite tax change,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2014\par 19:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, June 4 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real weakened to its\par lowest level in over two months on Wednesday, despite the\par removal of a tax that should encourage dollar inflows, as\par investors remained cautious over the outlook for future \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     Other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were weaker or little\par changed against the dollar, which rose globally on the back of\par higher \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  rates and a stronger U.S. ISM services sector\par reading.  \par     The real  lost ground for a fourth straight\par session, falling to 2.28 per dollar, also on the back of the\par U.S. data.\par     "The ISM services data came in better than expected and\par caused ... the real and other emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken,"\par said Luciano Rostagno, chief strategist at Banco Mizuho in Sao\par Paulo.\par     Earlier on Wednesday, Brazil's government announced the\par scrapping of a 6 percent financial tax, known as the IOF, on\par some short-term foreign loans, a move that Finance Minister\par Guido Mantega said would help normalize the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par  \par     The real has been volatile in recent sessions after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tried to slow down the pace at which it rolls over\par expiring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps, used by investors who wish to hedge\par themselves against a possible weakening of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     For a second straight day on Wednesday, the bank rolled over\par 10,000 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps - derivatives that let investors hedge\par against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses - after a sharp drop in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par Monday following its decision to roll over only half that\par amount.\par     "The dollar is rising abroad and there are some doubts about\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said a trader who declined to be named because\par he is not authorized to speak to the press. "Maybe with this IOF\par measure, if there are more inflows from here on, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could reduce its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . When you have uncertainty\par ahead, people prefer to stay cautious."\par     Forecasts for the real point to a gradual weakening of the\par Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to 2.47 per dollar in 12 months, according to\par Reuters' monthly survey of 31 strategists. \par     Elsewhere in Latin America, Chile's peso declined by\par the most in two weeks, driven by a drop of over 1 percent in the\par price of copper, the country's main export.\par     Stock markets tracked downward across the region, with the\par MSCI Latin American stock index retracing the\par previous two sessions' gains.\par     Brazil's benchmark Bovespa stock index dipped\par slightly, weighed down by data showing the country's industrial\par sector shrank for a second straight month in April.\par     Mexico's \f28 \uc2 \f2 IPC\f28 \uc2 \f2  index returned the previous session's\par gains, driven by a 0.7 percent fall in telecommunications firm\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 America Movil\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1634 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                 Latest        Daily   YTD pct\par                                                pct    change\par                                             change  \par  MSCI Emerging Markets          1,031.09     -0.47      3.32\par                                                     \par  MSCI LatAm                      3,234.4     -1.01      2.08\par                                                     \par  Brazil Bovespa                51,801.75     -0.44      0.57\par  Mexico \f28 \uc2 \f2 IPC\f28 \uc2 \f2                     41,896.65     -0.54     -1.94\par  Chile IPSA                     3,908.74     -0.14      5.66\par  Chile IGPA                    19,086.32     -0.05      4.71\par  Argentina MerVal               7,684.96      -0.3     42.55\par                                                     \par  Colombia IGBC                 13,738.14     -0.39      5.10\par  Peru IGRA                     15,817.07       0.4      0.40\par  Venezuela IBC                   2,163.5         0    -20.94\par                                                             \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                   Daily   YTD pct\par                                                pct    change\par                                   Latest    change  \par  Brazil real                      2.2846     -0.30      3.16\par  Mexico peso                     12.9438     -0.04      0.67\par  Chile peso                        552.7     -0.51     -4.81\par  Colombia peso                  1,898.49     -0.06      1.77\par  Peru sol                          2.7