\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real drops as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  slows swap rollover\b0\par\par\uc2 672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2014\par 17:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RIO DE JANEIRO, May 5 (Reuters) - Brazil's real weakened on\par Monday as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slowed the rollover of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par swaps, derivatives designed to support the exchange rate, that\par expire early next month.\par     Concerns about an economic deceleration in China and growing\par geopolitical tension in Ukraine contributed to the real's\par weakness and weighed on other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and stock\par markets, most of which were flat to lower.\par     The real  dropped 0.7 percent to 2.2328 per U.S.\par dollar following a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Friday announcement that it\par would start rolling over the $9.65 billion worth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par swaps that mature on June 2 with the offer of 5,000 new\par contracts on Monday.\par     In previous months, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  offered 10,000 new\par swaps a day to roll over expiring contracts.\par     "The reduction in the swap supply shows the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par comfortable with the real at current levels, said Reginaldo\par Siaca, a manager at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  desk of Advanced brokerage in\par Sao Paulo.\par     Tarcisio Rodrigues, director of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  desk at Banco\par Paulista in Sao Paulo, said dollars were flowing into Brazil on\par Monday, but concern about "Ukraine and China, as well as the\par reduced swap rollover by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , are weighing on the\par real."\par     Fear that China, the world's second-largest economy, may\par still be losing momentum increased after data showed the\par country's manufacturing sector contracted for a fourth\par consecutive month in April. China is a major destination for\par Latin America's commodities exports. \par     Investors were also cautiously watching the development of\par the crisis in Ukraine, where paramilitary police were killed in\par fighting with pro-Russian separatists near the rebel stronghold\par of Slaviansk. \par     Mexico's peso was little changed at 13.0105 per\par dollar, while the country's benchmark IPC stock index \par slid 0.1 percent.\par     Brazil's benchmark Bovespa index rose 0.4 percent,\par however, as investors continued to focus on opinion polls that\par showed President Dilma Rousseff has been losing popular support\par ahead of presidential elections in October. \par     Investors, who have blamed Rousseff's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par policies for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's low growth rates, are encouraged by the\par possibility of a more market-friendly government in 2015.\par     "The latest surveys show growing chances that we have a\par run-off vote in October," said Felipe Rocha, an analyst with\par Omar Camargo brokerage in Curitiba.\par     Brazil's latest electoral survey, released on Saturday,\par showed Rousseff losing ground to Senator Aecio Neves of the\par opposition PSDB party. The Bovespa index jumped 2.6 percent on\par Friday as investors anticipated that survey showing Rousseff's\par popularity falling. \par     Among the biggest gainers Monday on the Brazilian bourse,\par shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Prumo Logistica\f28 \uc2 \f2  jumped 5.4 percent after\par the company said it will lease part of its Port of Acu in the\par north of Rio de Janeiro to NFX, a joint-venture with \f28 \uc2 \f2 BP Plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par .\par  \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1537 GMT:\par      Stock indexes                     daily %    YTD %\par                             Latest     change     change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets    1000.23      -0.31      0.07\par                                                   \par  MSCI LatAm               3304.5       -0.26      3.51\par                                                   \par  Brazil Bovespa           53215.24     0.44       3.32\par                                                   \par  Mexico IPC               40927.27     -0.1       -4.21\par                                                   \par  Chile IPSA               3919.5       -0.26      5.96\par                                                   \par  Chile IGPA               19226.44     -0.18      5.48\par                                                   \par  Argentina MerVal         6889.94      1.59       27.80\par                                                   \par  Colombia IGBC            13470.3      -0.04      3.05\par                                                   \par  Peru IGRA                15629.52     0.37       -0.79\par                                                   \par  Venezuela IBC            2349.86      -0.63      -14.13\par                                                   \par                                                   \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             daily %    YTD %\par                                        change     change\par                           Latest                  \par  Brazil real              2.2328       -0.69      5.55\par                                                   \par