\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Little Changed as  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Offsets Growth Concern\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paulo Winterstein   \par \uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2014\par 19:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real was little changed on Monday as continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped contain weakness after economists whittled down their outlook for Latin America's biggest economy and the release of data showing slower-than-expected global economic activity.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.3761 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with BRL2.3779 at Friday's close.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian economists surveyed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said economic growth last year likely reached 2.28%, down from a previous forecast of 2.3% growth. This year, growth is expected to slow even more, with the economy expanding 1.95% in 2014, down from a previous estimate of 2%, according to the weekly survey.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Brazil's biggest trading partner, China, also posted disappointing economic data on Monday. The HSBC China services Purchasing Managers' Index fell to 50.9 in December from 52.5 in November, with growth in new orders the lowest in six months, \uc2 HSBC Holdings PLC\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Europe and the U.S. also released PMI data. In Europe, the figure showed a slight drop to 51.0 in December, in line with estimates, while in the U.S. the number slipped to 55.7.\par \par \uc2 Despite the soft data, the real didn't repeat losses seen last week, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched 2.4 against the dollar. According to the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey, the real is expected to weaken to 2.45 to the dollar by year end.\par \par \uc2 Further declines were prevented by continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would continue holding regular auctions to supply dollar credit lines and foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts that help investors increase \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  predictability. By allowing investors to hedge against future swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there is less immediate demand for investors to buy dollars and thereby less weakness in the real.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold about $200 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts.\par \par \uc2 Some have criticized the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to reduce the scale of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets. However, for analysts such as \uc2 Banco Santander\uc2  economist Adriana Dupita, the less intensive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could allow for longer-lasting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Had the [\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] opted for a more aggressive swap program instead, simple math would lead markets and rating agencies to question, at some point, the country's ability to preserve this status in the event there is a longer-than-announced swap program," the economist wrote.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 06, 2014 13:47 ET (18:47 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140106ea16002ja\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
