\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil, Mexico  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  dip as Treasuries yields rise\b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2013\par 13:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Dec 27 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Mexico and Brazil edged lower in thin holiday trading on Friday as yields on 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  notes rose above 3 percent for the first time since September, potentially encouraging investors to exit riskier emerging markets. Concern about the pace of withdrawal of U.S. monetary stimulus, which could drive Treasuries yields higher, are expected to weigh on Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  next year. The U.S. Federal Reserve will scale back its bond-buying program by $10 billion to $75 billion a month as of next year, and future cuts will depend on the pace of recovery of the U.S. economy. * Brazil's real dropped 0.1 percent after three consecutive sessions of gains. It has weakened over 13 percent so far this year even as losses have been cushioned by heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday offered as much as $1.66 billion on the spot market with repurchase agreement set to May 4, 2014. That auction is intended at rolling over similar dollar lines that are about to expire. * Later this morning, as part of its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will offer as much as $1 billion on the spot market with repurchase date set to June 3, 2014. * Brazilian policymakers will halve their \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program in 2014, a move that will make the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more vulnerable to the withdrawal of the Fed's stimulus, analysts say. * Mexico's peso , Latin America's most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , weakened 0.2 percent. It has posted losses during five of the past six sessions as speculation about the future of U.S. stimulus takes a tool in emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . * Chile's peso rose 0.2 percent as the price of copper, the country's main export product, reached a four-month high on the London Metal Exchange. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1205 GMT:\par     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          daily %    YTD %\par                                      change   change\par                             Latest           \par  Brazil real                2.3561    -0.11   -13.42\par                                              \par  Mexico peso               13.1100    -0.19    -1.87\par                                              \par  Chile peso               523.4000     0.21    -8.54\par                                              \par  Peru sol                   2.7850     0.00    -8.40\par                                              \par  Argentina peso             6.4700    -0.43   -24.07\par  (interbank)                                 \par                                              \par  Argentina peso             9.9200    -2.22   -31.65\par  (parallel)                                  \par                                              \par  \par     \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Walter Brandimarte; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | M | RBN | RNP | DNP | P