\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank \highlight\uc2  to slow pace of  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2013\par 23:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to offer $200 mln worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps per day\par \par \uc2 * Dollar sales through repos will hinge on market liquidity\par \par \uc2 * Additional dollar sales may happen if needed (Adds background, comment from finance minister)\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Dec 18 (Reuters) - \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Wednesday a likely slowdown in the pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  next year, a move that appears aimed at taking advantage of an upbeat market reaction to U.S. policymakers' decision to cut back on monetary stimulus.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement that it will extend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program with some adjustments through at least the end of the first half of 2014.\par \par \uc2 The program extension will provide investors with some $20 billion worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivatives that offer protection against a possible depreciation of the real. That compares to about $60 billion in swaps offered in the first leg of the program, which went into effect at the end of August.\par \par \uc2 The adjustment in the pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was announced after markets reacted positively to the Fed's decision to cut its $85 billion-a-month bond-buying program by an initial $10 billion as of next year.\par \par \uc2 Even as the decision could reduce the supply of dollars seeking higher returns in emerging markets, investors were encouraged by the Fed's suggestion that U.S. interest rates may remain near zero for longer than expected.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Guido Mantega, who earlier on Friday had called on U.S. policymakers to start cutting the stimulus sooner rather than later, said the first indications were that Brazilian markets were reacting well to the Fed's decision.\par \par \uc2 "That means we'll have less turbulence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. It means the dollar will strengthen less (against the real) than some maybe expected," he said in an interview with Globo TV.\par \par \uc2 $200 MILLION A DAY\par \par \uc2 Including previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year, the stock of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps offered by \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to reach $100 billion at the end of 2013 and $120 billion by the end of June 2014, or about one-third of the country's international reserves of $375 billion.\par \par \uc2 As of next year, the bank will offer $200 million a day worth of traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, or $1 billion per week through its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program. That is half the $2 billion it currently offers every week in auctions held from Mondays through Thursdays.\par \par \uc2 Dollar sales on the spot market through repurchase agreements will "depend on liquidity conditions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added in the statement.\par \par \uc2 Currently, policymakers offer as much as $1 billion worth of dollar repos on Fridays, but government sources have told Reuters that demand for such dollar lines has not been very strong.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said, however, that it may still sell dollars through "all instruments available" whenever it deems it necessary, leaving the door open for more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program was announced when the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded around 2.45 per dollar in late August, adding to inflation pressures. It has greatly contributed to stabilizing the real around the current level of 2.3 per dollar. (Additional reporting by Brad Haynes; Editing by Todd Benson, Andrew Hay and Ken Wills)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | M | NAT | ABX | BNX | FUN | C | E | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131221e9ci000af\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
