\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Strengthens Early Ahead Of U.S. Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2013\par 12:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real strengthened in early trading Thursday as investors awaited clues to the path of U.S. policy ahead of U.S. retail data scheduled for release during the session.\par \par \uc2 As of 6:05 a.m. EST, the real traded at BRL2.3342 to the dollar after ending at BRL2.3381 to the dollar Wednesday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the real has shown volatility in recent sessions while the market awaits the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision on whether to renew its $85 billion per month bond purchasing program.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to discontinue the program, investors await November retail data due from the U.S. to gauge whether the timing will be right for the move.\par \par \uc2 According to market expectations, retail sales are seen advancing by about 0.6% during the month after a 0.4% increase in October.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's decision on bond purchases, meanwhile, is expected in its report next week.\par \par \uc2 Local investors in Brazil note the Fed's path should be critical for Brazil's own \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy moves, and whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's own \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will renew its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling a daily "ration" of about $500 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps since August as a measure to curb excess volatility and local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening ahead of expected changes in Fed policy.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian officials have said they are prepared to continue the swap sales if necessary, though Brazilian Finance Minister Guido Mantega said Wednesday the next move would likely depend on the Fed's position.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 12, 2013 06:31 ET (11:31 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131212e9cc0018i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
