\par\par \b \uc2 South Korean Won, Indian Rupee Lead Rally in Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2013\par 20:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won and the Indian rupee posted gains Monday as the dollar weakened against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 China's trade surplus, reported over the weekend, showed its biggest gain in five years. This gave investors a rosier read on the global economy and demand from China leading to a rebound in confidence and of higher yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the won, rupee and the Brazilian real.\par \par \uc2 The Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to its strongest level to the dollar since January as the country draws more investors based on its steady economic outlook, low inflation and current-account surplus. The dollar fell to KRW1049.1 during the day, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Also, \uc2 South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to meet this week and keep rates on hold at 2.5%. At the same time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep a close eye on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and it will be a test to see how low they let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  go before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the real, which had weakened in previous weeks. The real gained 0.56% to the dollar Monday, to trade at BRL2.3160, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee gained on local factors too, as the country's main opposition party won in local elections. Many market participants viewed this as a precursor to national elections to be held next week, and anticipate the transition to a more market-friendly regime. The dollar fell to INR60.80 during the day, a four-month low for the greenback against the rupee. Currently, the rupee trades at INR60.98, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, promise of reforms in Mexico gave a boost to that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which strengthened to MXN12.8646 per dollar. The peso gained 1.5% to the dollar last week.\par \par \uc2 Mexico, increasingly, is featuring in emerging-market investors bets for next year. The country is focused on fixing its energy policy and the congressional discussion on the subject began Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 09, 2013 14:55 ET (19:55 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131209e9c9002va\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
