\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Strengthens on Continued  \highlight22\uc2 Central-Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2013\par 20:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real strengthened against the dollar Monday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and as strong economic data from China, Brazil's biggest trading partner, helped lift global markets.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading against the dollar at BRL2.3169, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, stronger than Friday's close at BRL2.3278.\par \par \uc2 China posted its biggest trade surplus in almost five years in November. Exports rebounded in what many economists see as a positive sign for the global economy and China, even as imports grew at a smaller pace.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its policy of offering foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts that allow investors to hedge against swings in the real. Last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Alexandre Tombini said that the government will extend into next year its offer of those contracts.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a banking sector event in Sao Paulo on Thursday, Mr. Tombini said that "with adjustments, we will keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedge program in place in 2014."\par \par \uc2 With the prospect of the U.S. Federal Reserve slowing down its bond-buying program, emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have taken a hit. The bond-buying program allowed investors to buy more overseas assets as the cost of borrowing in dollars fell, which in turn drove up prices and strengthened \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the real. Because a weak real could pressure inflation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure stability in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For Monday, the bank rolled over $1 billion in expiring contracts and sold about $500 million in new contracts.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week also released minutes of its most recent interest-rate decision meeting, when it raised the Selic rate by half a point, as expected. Coming shortly before disappointing third-quarter gross domestic product data, the rate decision cemented expectations that growth in Brazil will continue to slow.\par \par \uc2 A weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey of economists showed a decline in growth expectations for this year and next.\par \par \uc2 The 100 respondents in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey cut their outlook for the country's economic expansion for 2013 to 2.35% from 2.50% and for next year to 2.10% from 2.11%.\par \par \uc2 The survey respondents reduced their inflation forecast for the end of 2013 to 5.70% from 5.81%, while keeping 2014 estimates steady.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 09, 2013 14:07 ET (19:07 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131209e9c9002mb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
