\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Stronger on  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Rally\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2013\par 20:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--The Brazilian real closed sharply stronger against the dollar intraday Friday, as comments from a senior Federal Reserve official backed the institution's monetary stimulus programs and \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vowed to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in coming months.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.3278 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with BRL2.3593 at Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 Chicago Fed President Charles Evans said Friday that data showing U.S. unemployment at a five-year low probably overstates the improvement in the economy and supported a continuation of the Fed's bond-buying programs. Brazilian assets have benefitted from the so-called quantitative easing measures and have proven sensitive in recent months to talk of their rollback.\par \par \uc2 Also propping up the real, Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Alexandre Tombini said Thursday that the bank will continue into next year a dollar-hedging program that had been slated to expire at the end of 2013. The program offers up to $500 million per day in swap contracts, allowing investors to lock in future dollar prices without stocking up on hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "They're going to guarantee liquidity to the market," said Reginaldo Galhardo, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Sao Paulo's Treviso brokerage.\par \par \uc2 Mauricio Gaioti, a trader at Ouro Minas in Sao Paulo, said investor positioning on Brazil's futures market has turned heavily in favor of the real versus the dollar since Mr. Tombini's announcement.\par \par \uc2 "The shadow of the government continues to influence the market," he said. "Brazil has a clear policy of not letting the exchange rate rise out of control."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has using daily, scheduled swap auctions since August, when the real spiraled to its weakest levels against the dollar--around BRL2.45--in several years amid expectations that the Fed would start rolling back its bond purchases and amid trouble in Brazil's economy.\par \par \uc2 The latter issue has deepened in recent months, with the economy contracting 0.5% in the third quarter, the largest margin since early 2009. Economists worry that next year's presidential elections could further delay badly needed reforms.\par \par \uc2 "Independent of the result of the elections, we expect there to be a tightening of fiscal and monetary policies in 2015," economists at Banco J. Safra said in a special report Thursday evening.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paul Kiernan at paul.kiernan@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 06, 2013 14:14 ET (19:14 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131206e9c600310\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
