\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Brazil to extend  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  program on concern over inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2013\par 16:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds more comments from Tombini, background)\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Dec 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will extend its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program into 2014, with some adjustments, to curb market volatility that could limit the impact of monetary policy over inflation, bank chief \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "I announce that, with some adjustments, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will extend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap program," Tombini told a crowd of banking executives in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Tombini said the recent volatility seen in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets could make the impact of monetary policy over inflation more uncertain.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real added to early gains and rallied 1.3 percent after Tombini's comments.\par \par \uc2 Launched on Aug. 22, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program has helped curb volatility in the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which has become more volatile due to concern over the timing of withdrawal of U.S. stimulus measures. (Reporting by Eric Sukys; Writing by Alonso Soto; Editing by James Dalgleish, Walter Brandimarte and Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | M | NAT | D | E | RBN | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokumen