\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Gains As  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Promises More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paulo Winterstein   \par \uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2013\par 19:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real strengthened against the dollar Thursday for the first time in five days after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will continue offering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedge options next year.\par \par \uc2 After opening somewhat weaker, the real reversed direction and exited active trading at BRL2.3593 to the dollar, stronger than Wednesday's close of BRL2.3796 according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a banking sector event in Sao Paulo on Thursday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Alexandre Tombini said that a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -hedging program that was promised through the end of this year will be extended into next year. In August, the bank introduced a program of daily auctions of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -swap contracts meant to reduce volatility as the Brazilian real lost value against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The hedges have the practical effect of strengthening the real. By purchasing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -hedge contracts, investors can lock in future dollar prices, eliminating the need to stock up on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to safeguard against future swings in prices.\par \par \uc2 "In 2014 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't exit this market," Mr. Tombini said, according to a transcript of his speech posted on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website. "With some adjustments, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will extend the program offering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tombini's speech came after the bank published minutes of its most recent interest-rate decision. Last week, the bank raised rates by half a point to 10%, as expected. On Thursday, minutes showed a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerned with increasing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. Such volatility puts inflation control at risk, the bank has noted several times.\par \par \uc2 The minutes also hinted that Brazil could slow its pace of rate increases as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gives time for past rate hikes to take effect.\par \par \uc2 The possible slowdown in rates comes at a difficult time, as the country is still seeing inflation close to the upper limits of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target, which ranges from 2.5% to 6.5%. Inflation currently stands at around 5.8%, and investors expect it to remain steady through the end of next year. In minutes of the meeting, the bank said that inflation will likely stay close to the upper end of the band through the third quarter of 2015.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 05, 2013 13:45 ET (18:45 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131205e9c5002zf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
