\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Ends Weaker On Upbeat Data Abroad\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2013\par 20:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real lost ground against the dollar to end weaker Wednesday as economic data abroad outweighed the influence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a likely interest rate increase locally.\par \par \uc2 The real exited regular trading at BRL2.3167 to the dollar after ending at BRL2.2932 to the dollar Tuesday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 The real began the session moving weaker and further lost ground throughout the day as data in the U.S. ahead of the Thanksgiving holiday pointed to a growing likelihood the Federal Reserve could soon end a monetary stimulus program.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted improvements in U.S. jobless claims and the Chicago industrial activity index added fuel to speculation investors would divert money from emerging markets such as Brazil in search of rising returns abroad.\par \par \uc2 "In the coming year the market agenda will be headlined by effects of a reduction in the Fed's monetary stimulus program, which has already been prompting the withdrawal of some funds from the country," said Sidnei Nehme, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at the NGO brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The real's weakening movement, meanwhile, was little swayed by continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold more than $1.5 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps at two auctions Wednesday as part of its ongoing effort to provide dollar liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The bank Wednesday evening is expected to raise the country's benchmark Selic interest rate by half a percentage point to 10% annually to help curb inflation that has recently approached 6%.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 27, 2013 14:36 ET (19:36 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131127e9br0030k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
