\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens Stronger on  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2013\par 13:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real opened moderately stronger against the dollar Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it planned to roll over $1 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts expiring soon.\par \par \uc2 At 7 a.m. EST, the real was quoted at BRL2.3257 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with BRL2.3339 at Wednesday's close.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has depreciated by about 6.5% in the past month as better-than-expected economic data from the U.S. renewed concerns about the tapering, or winding down, of the Federal Reserve's $85 billion monthly bond-buying program.\par \par \uc2 But the real has been more or less stable in recent sessions, reflecting expectations that the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step into the market to prevent further weakness that might exacerbate inflationary pressure.\par \par \uc2 The bank said late Wednesday it will offer up to $1 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts, a mechanism used by authorities to send the real stronger against the dollar, as part of an effort to roll over the $10.25 billion in swaps coming due Dec. 2.\par \par \uc2 The auction is scheduled for 2:30 p.m. (1630 GMT) local time.\par \par \uc2 Reginaldo Siaca, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Sao Paulo's Advanced brokerage, said he doesn't expect any big movements during Thursday's session, the last of the week in Brazil because of a holiday weekend. Beyond that, he sees the real getting stronger.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think the government is going to let the real get much weaker, as it could drive up inflation," Mr. Siaca said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paul Kiernan at paul.kiernan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 14, 2013 07:28 ET (12:28 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131114e9be001uc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
