\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Yellen's defense of Fed stimulus buoys Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2013\par 15:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Nov 14 (Reuters) - Brazil's real had its biggest jump in a month on Thursday on signals that the U.S. Federal Reserve will keep its stimulus intact until it sees a strong recovery and after \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended its rollover of expiring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps. The real gained 0.58 percent to 2.3209 per U.S. dollar, its biggest session gain since mid October, after Fed chair nominee \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  defended the Fed's $85 billion\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monthly bond-buying stimulus program.  \par     Speaking at a Senate hearing on Thursday, Yellen said she\par would press forward with the Fed's ultra-easy monetary policy\par until officials were confident a durable economic recovery was\par in place that could sustain job creation. \par     "Yellen's speech signaled the stimulus will be maintained,\par reducing expectations for tapering in December. This is what\par weakened the dollar here," said Caio Sasaki, head of analysis at\par brokerage XP Investimentos in Sao Paulo.\par     The Fed's program has buoyed investor appetite for riskier,\par high-yielding emerging-market assets. \par     The real, which is still down more than 12 percent this\par year, snapped its seven-session losing streak on Thursday thanks\par also to continued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. \par     Brazilian policymakers have been regularly selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par swaps as part of a daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program that provides\par investors with a hedge against a possible depreciation of the\par real, helping reduce demand for dollars on the spot market.\par     With $10.1 billion worth of swaps due to expire on Dec. 2,\par the bank has been conducting rollover auctions since Tuesday.\par The bank rolled over 20,000 contracts, equivalent to about $1\par billion, in an auction on Thursday.\par     The Mexican peso firmed 0.48 percent to close at\par 12.9625 per dollar, its strongest close since last October and\par its third consecutive session of gains.\par     Mexico's lower house of Congress early on Thursday passed\par the federal spending plan for next year, completing approval for\par the budget, which proposes running a deficit in 2014 to lift the\par country's struggling economy. \par     \par     Latin America \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prices at 2204 GMT:\par       \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                  daily %      YTD %\par                                              change     change\par                                   Latest             \par  Brazil real                     2.3209        0.58     -12.10\par                                                      \par  Mexico peso                     12.9625       0.48      -0.76\par                                                      \par  Chile peso                     518.8000       0.27      -7.73\par                                                      \par  Colombia peso                 1925.5000       0.47      -8.28\par                                                      \par  Peru sol                         2.7980       0.07      -8.83\par                                                      \par  Argentina peso (interbank)       5.9875      -0.17     -17.95\par                                                      \par  Argentina peso (parallel)        9.9500      -0.50     -31.86\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131114e9be0011y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
