\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens Stronger on  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paulo Winterstein   \par \uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2013\par 13:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real strengthened against the dollar in early Wednesday trading as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  intensified \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after the real touched a two-week low against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The real was trading at 2.3224 per dollar at 7:00 EST, after closing at BRL2.3314 to the dollar on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 After markets closed on Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced plans to hold an auction of new foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts as well as contracts to replace those expiring at the start of next month. The bank plans to sell up to $1.5 billion in new contracts, whereas a week ago the bank was selling just $500 million a day in regular auctions.\par \par \uc2 Whereas the bank waited until the end of October to roll over contracts expiring Nov. 1, this time the bank has been rolling over contracts maturing Dec. 2 since the start of the month. Traders say that the earlier rollover has assuaged investor fears that not all the contracts would be rolled over. Last month, the bank only rolled over about two-thirds of the almost $9 billion in maturing contracts. In December, about $10 billion in contracts mature.\par \par \uc2 The stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped staunch sudden weakness in the real. Last week the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid against the dollar after strong jobs data revived speculation that the U.S. Federal Reserve could start tapering its bond-buying program this year. The bond-buying program made borrowing in dollars cheaper, and as a result pushed up the prices of global assets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The possible reversal of stimulus policies in the U.S. comes at a time when Brazilian government accounts are deteriorating and doubts are rising about the willingness and ability of the federal government to slow spending. With presidential elections coming up next year in Brazil, many analysts are concerned spending will pick up, further unbalancing the country's accounts and possibly leading to a cut in the country's credit rating.\par \par \uc2 -Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 13, 2013 07:19 ET (12:19 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131113e9bd001lz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
