\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Slightly Stronger on Stepped-up  \highlight22\uc2 Central-Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2013\par 19:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real was slightly stronger Tuesday after two separate auctions of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts by the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real ended active trading at BRL2.3314 against the U.S. dollar, slightly stronger than Monday's close of BRL2.3335, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the equivalent of nearly $1.5 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts at two auctions Tuesday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month were limited, on most trading days, to a single auction of about $500 million.\par \par \uc2 The contracts tend to support the real against the dollar by giving investors the opportunity to exchange bonds linked to domestic interest rates for paper indexed directly to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to traders, much of the reason for the stepped-up \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to do with the expiry of some $10.25 billion in swap contracts on Dec. 2.\par \par \uc2 "The market is now convinced that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  intends to replace the entire amount coming due on Dec. 2," said Ricardo Gomes da Silva, a trader at the Correparti brokerage in southern Brazil.\par \par \uc2 In October, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  replaced only a portion of swap contracts expiring on Nov. 1. In October, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $6 billion in new contracts against $8.9 billion that expired on Nov. 1.\par \par \uc2 The real was also strengthened Tuesday on sales of dollars held by exporters.\par \par \uc2 "The real weakened to as low as BRL2.34 on Monday, but that was an attractive rate for exporters to sell dollars," said Durval Correa, a trader at Sao Paulo's Multi Money brokerage.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tom Murphy at tom.murphy@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 12, 2013 13:54 ET (18:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131112e9bc003jv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
