\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Ends Weaker as Market Monitors Fed's Path\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2013\par 20:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real lost ground against the dollar to end weaker Friday as factors abroad, including recent signals from the U.S. Federal Reserve on policy, weighed against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real exited regular trading at BRL2.2548 to the dollar, after ending at BRL2.2287 to the dollar Thursday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the real began the session slipping against the greenback as local data and year-end demand for dollars influenced the market.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's IBGE statistics institute reported local industrial production came in below forecasts. Industrial output rose 0.7% during the month, a figure below projections of around 1.2%.\par \par \uc2 The soft output data is seen as possibly limiting any tightening of the local interest rate by \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and thus continuing to help bring investment dollars into the economy.\par \par \uc2 But concerns abroad brought still more pressure against the real throughout the session as investors fretted over possible interest-rate tightening in China and the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Worries over the Fed were causing particular waves after authorities there hinted this week that the institution could act soon to curb its stimulus policies.\par \par \uc2 "The market knows that this stimulus can't continue indefinitely," said Reginaldo Galhardo, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at the Treviso brokerage in Sao Paulo. "At some point there will have to be an adjustment.\par \par \uc2 Locally, meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's own \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen maintaining its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and weekly dollar lending to help provide liquidity and hedge.\par \par \uc2 The bank Friday held its weekly auction of $1 billion in dollar credit. The bank sold dollars at BRL2.2522 under agreement to repurchase them at BRL2.3165.\par \par \uc2 The bank in August agreed to extend approximately $100 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and dollar credit lines to the market through the end of this year, in order to curb excess depreciation of the real due to possible policy changes at the Fed and shifting flows of global investment capital. \par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 01, 2013 15:29 ET (19:29 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131101e9b10034j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
