\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens Weaker on Fed Bets, Easing  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paulo Winterstein   \par \uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2013\par 13:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real slipped against the dollar in early Thursday trading as speculation mounts that the U.S. may reverse stimulus policies soon, while in Brazil more investors see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  easing back its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real was at 2.1965 in morning trading, after closing at BRL2.1906 on Wednesday, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to BRL2.2 per dollar in intraday trading as investors see signs that the Federal Reserve could start tapering its bond-buying program as soon as December.\par \par \uc2 The monetary policy panel of the U.S. Federal Reserve Bank sent mixed signals on Wednesday when it said that the country's housing recovery has "slowed somewhat," while eliminating references to rising mortgage rates dragging down the economy.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has signaled that it may slow the pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In addition to carrying out daily foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions, where it offers investors a hedge against swings in the real, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been rolling over part of the almost $9 billion in existing swap contracts that expire Friday.\par \par \uc2 "There's been a lot of speculation on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will roll over all the swaps," said Anderson Rodrigues, a fixed-income manager at Daycoval Asset Management in Sao Paulo. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been testing the market a lot, saying that it wouldn't carry out an auction, then gauging market appetite for future auctions. It looks like they're trying to keep the real at current levels" of about BRL2.2 per dollar, he said.\par \par \uc2 As of Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had rolled over about $6 billion of the roughly $9 billion in contracts coming due. For Thursday, there were no rollover auctions announced.\par \par \uc2 The sharply widening deficit reported Thursday morning also helped weaken the real, Mr. Rodrigues said. Brazil's treasury reported a central government deficit of BRL10.47 billion, wider than the BRL432 million deficit posted in August.\par \par \uc2 -Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 31, 2013 08:47 ET (12:47 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131031e9av002ao\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
