\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weaker As Importers, Companies Buy Cheap Dollars\b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2013\par 20:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real weakened Wednesday as importers and companies with dollar-linked debts bought "cheap" U.S. dollars.\par \par \uc2 The real ended active trading at BRL2.1841 against the U.S. dollar, weaker against Tuesday's close of BRL2.1697, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Traders said a range of BRL2.15 to BRL2.17 against the dollar makes the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  look "cheap" to those needing dollars. Dollars were selling for BRL2.22 at the beginning of October. Importers and companies facing U.S. dollar payments in the coming days snapped up greenbacks Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The market was also betting that \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't rollover all of the $8.9 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts expiring on Nov. 1. The swap contracts tend to support the real against the dollar by giving investors an added hedge in the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Rolling over only a portion of the swaps, while allowing the rest to close out, will diminish hedging capability in the market and could strengthen the dollar in the next few days, traders said.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rolled over $1 billion in swaps, then another $1 billion Wednesday. Later Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will announce details of a third, and last, scheduled auction of rollover swaps set for Thursday. Investors are anxious to see how close the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will come to rolling over the $8.9 billion in swaps expiring next week.\par \par \uc2 "It's unlikely the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will offer the equivalent of $7 billion in new swaps on Thursday," said Joao Paulo de Gracia Correa, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager of the Correparti brokerage in southern \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "That would be too much \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at one time."\par \par \uc2 Write to Tom Murphy at tom.murphy@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 23, 2013 14:26 ET (18:26 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131023e9an004ae\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
