\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2 's delay in announcing swap auction weighs on real\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2013\par 21:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Oct 16 (Reuters) - Brazil's real trimmed its gains to close only modestly stronger on Wednesday as a delay in the announcement of an expected swap auction by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered speculation that policymakers were reviewing their program of daily \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been auctioning as many as 10,000 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps on Mondays through Thursdays as part of a $60 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program designed to provide investors with protection against a possible depreciation of the real.\par \par \uc2 Doubts about the swap offering increased, however, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to announce, before markets closed on Wednesday, the details of the contracts that would be sold on the following day.\par \par \uc2 The bank usually issues a statement with such details around 2:30 p.m. local time (1730 GMT) on the day prior to the sale. This time, however, that statement was only released after 8 p.m., when the bank announced it would sell on Thursday 10,000 traditional swap contracts maturing on March 5, 2014.\par \par \uc2 That came too late to ease the pressure on the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however. After rallying over 1 percent to a four-month high of 2.1551 per dollar during the session, the real closed only 0.2 percent stronger at 2.1735, lagging other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although many investors believe the government is not completely comfortable with the recent strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  has repeatedly said that the current \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program is working as expected and will last until the end of the year at least.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-REAL/ (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | U | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131016e9ag000vg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
