\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Weaker as Market Questions  \highlight22\uc2 Central-Bank Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tom Murphy   \par \uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2013\par 21:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real weakened Tuesday as investors increasingly questioned the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real ended active trading at BRL2.1812 against the U.S. dollar, weaker against the Monday close of BRL2.1743, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Traders said investors bought dollars late in the session on continued worries about the U.S. fiscal crisis. Traders noted that market volume Tuesday was low.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on a daily basis since August 22 by selling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and U.S. dollar credit lines. The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have the effect of replenishing dollar supplies to the market and supporting the real against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, many investors and analysts question the need for continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real has lost about 9% against the U.S. dollar so far this year. According to most economists, the depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is contributing to Brazil's worrisome 6% inflation rate. However, on the other hand, an even weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would help make Brazilian exports more competitive.\par \par \uc2 For the moment, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems focused more on the inflation problem than on foreign trade, according to economists. For that reason, the bank has adopted a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the real. Daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are due to continue through the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 In a research note, economists at Sao Paulo's LCA consulting group said that, without daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real would likely weaken to about BRL2.25 against the dollar, giving a boost to exports.\par \par \uc2 Other economists suggest that winding down \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a desirable policy move.\par \par \uc2 In their own research note, economists at private bank Itau said a gradual reduction in the volume of daily swaps and credit lines would help promote a modest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation that would make Brazilian exports more competitive. They suggested there was a possibility of such a policy change.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the mere idea that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could scale back on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has now become a market factor in itself, according to Vanderlei Muniz, a partner in southern Brazil's Onnix brokerage. "At BRL2.17 or BRL2.18, buyers think the dollar is cheap," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tom Murphy at tom.murphy@dowjones.com [ 15-10-13 1938GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020131015e9af000ne\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
