\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Tombini: Decline in Inflation to Continue in 2014\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paulo Trevisani and Paulo Winterstein   \par \uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2013\par 20:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Washington, D.C.--\uc2 Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  on Friday reinforced his view that Brazil's inflation will decline this year and next, just two days after the bank raised interest rates for a fifth time this year, and said that U.S. talks on its debt ceiling are causing "great concern" among policy makers.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is committed to bringing inflation down," he told reporters in Washington, D.C., following a meeting with fellow central bankers. "We will have lower inflation this year than last year and continue experiencing lower inflation in Brazil next year."\par \par \uc2 As was widely expected, Brazil raised rates to 9.5% on Wednesday. In a statement accompanying the decision, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained the same wording it used during previous decisions, keeping the door open for additional rate hikes. Many analysts had expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to give some sign that the cycle of increases were coming to a close as Brazilian growth sputters and inflation shows some sign of retreat.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tombini declined to comment on what the statement means for future rate decisions, saying only that minutes of the meeting that will be released Oct. 17 could provide more clarity.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tombini said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also monitor closely decisions by the Federal Reserve and by the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  that could affect future monetary policy. The Fed has signaled it will continue through the end of this year with its current bond-buying program--a program that helped drive investment to emerging economies and strengthen their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Meanwhile, Congress is deadlocked on talks to end a government shutdown, which could have ramifications in concurrent talks to raise the country's debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 "The debt ceiling talks are important," Mr. Tombini said. "During our meeting they were asked about this and it's a subject that has caused great concern."\par \par \uc2 "It's an exorbitant risk for the world economy," he said.\par \par \uc2 Concern about the Fed program and the debt ceiling have caused some upheavals in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but Mr. Tombini praised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for helping reduce wild swings. The government announced in August that it would inject about $60 billion into the market via \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and credit lines. That helped strengthen the real after it touched a four year-low against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Asked about \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 's nomination to head the Fed, Mr. Tombini said that he knows her well from having worked with her for several years during his time at \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but declined to comment further.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Trevisani and Paulo Winterstein at brazil@dowjones.com [ 10-11-13 1430ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020131011e9ab0003l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
