\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weakens Slightly; U.S. Debt Row, Rates in Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2013\par 22:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real slipped against the dollar to end slightly weaker Tuesday, while investors maintained a conservative strategy amid doubts surrounding a lingering impasse over debt in the U.S. and the outlook for interest rates locally.\par \par \uc2 The real exited regular trading at BRL2.2044 to the dollar after ending at BRL2.2042 to the dollar Monday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began the session moving stronger against the dollar, but held within a narrow range as investors struggled to identify longer-term market trends.\par \par \uc2 Still at the forefront of concerns were the implications of stalled talks in the U.S. on a government shutdown and the possible increase of the debt ceiling. Analysts noted that while the political dispute continues, the U.S. Federal Reserve is likely to prolong its loose monetary policy that has helped irrigate emerging markets like Brazil with dollars.\par \par \uc2 Locally, meanwhile, investors are considering the impact of likely continued interest rate hikes and their capacity to attract more incoming investment.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to raise the country's benchmark Selic interest rate again this week, hiking it by as much as half a percentage point from its current 9% to curb inflation.\par \par \uc2 However, market observers note that so far \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buoyed by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of some $500 million per day and still ample foreign reserves of more than $370 billion.\par \par \uc2 "Thanks to this cushion and the swap program, the real was the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that most appreciated in emerging markets since the peak of depreciation in August," noted strategist Paulo Gala at \uc2 Banco Fator\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Questions remain, however, about whether Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain its recent strength ahead given the country's still widening current account deficit and the possibility that the Fed could back away from its ongoing loose-money policies once a political impasse over the U.S. budget is resolved.\par \par \uc2 But until clearer signs appear on that front, traders said they expect Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold within a range of BRL2.20 to BRL2.25 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 08-10-13 2015GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020131008e9a8000mr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
