\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Stronger Agaist Dollar on U.S. Shutdown, Debt Ceiling\b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2013\par 21:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened slightly against the dollar Monday as constant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  calmed investor jitters ahead of a looming U.S. deadline to lift the country's debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.2042 against the U.S. dollar, somewhat stronger than Friday's close of BRL2.2079, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 As the U.S. enters the second week of its shutdown, all eyes are turned to the Oct. 17 deadline when the government must approve a new debt limit or risk running out of money to pay bills, including servicing its debt.\par \par \uc2 "Trading volume has been small as the market is in wait-and-see mode in relation to the U.S.," said Jose Carlos Amado, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Renascenca brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 With the low trading volume, even small inflows of $50 million to Brazil have an impact on the market, which likely explains some of the day's volatility, Mr. Amado said. The real weakened to BRL2.2186 per greenback in the morning, and strengthened to as much as BRL2.2015 in afternoon trading.\par \par \uc2 Most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened against the greenback as a resolution to the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  shutdown still seems remote. On Sunday, U.S. House Speaker \uc2 John Boehner\uc2  said the government wouldn't return to normal until Democrats agree to broader talks aimed at reducing the country's deficit.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets daily in order to ensure that investor demand for dollars is met.\par \par \uc2 "The market has been working at this level of BRL2.20 to BRL2.22, with investors selling [dollars] when the real weakens beyond that and buying when it strengthens," Mr. Amado said. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been continuing its program and that leaves traders more comfortable."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps at regularly scheduled auctions since August. The auctions tend to support the Brazilian real by giving investors added opportunities to hedge in dollars.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@wsj.com [ 10-07-13 1545ET ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020131007e9a70003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
